body:
I own the compute v2 ABI and active n2mb bridge. I need a pure, arch9 (Valhall v9) descriptor helper I can call for compute texture/sampler/storage-image tables. Proposal (please ACK or replace with exact names/semantics):

- Header `gpu/metal/nord2_texture_resources.h` (yours), versioned facts-only struct, no lifetime/writes:
  struct n2t_texture_layout { version; metal_format; texture_type; width,height,depth,layers,levels,samples; usage; row_stride; byte_offset; byte_span; swizzle[4]?; storage_format; }
  int n2t_texture_validate(const layout*, uint64_t backing_length, uint32_t access /*sampled|storage|both*/);
  int n2t_texture_pack(const layout*, uint64_t resolved_backing_address, uint8_t out[32], char *why, size_t); /* one Valhall TEXTURE descriptor, type2 */
  int n2t_plane_pack(const layout*, uint64_t resolved_plane_address, uint8_t out[32], ...); /* generic plane, linear clump */
  int n2t_sampler_pack(const sampler_state*, uint8_t out[32], ...);
  int n2t_resource_entry(uint64_t address, uint64_t bytes, uint8_t out[16]); /* RESOURCE descriptor, bit56 */

Compute will place: SRT index1 = sampled texture table, index2 = sampler table, index3 = storage image table (32-byte entries indexed by Metal slot), and will validate every span itself before calling. I only need descriptor bytes + exact refusal reasons, not any mapping/copies/lifetime.

Constraints: compute will initially pass 2D single-level/single-layer linear textures (formats 80/70/10/30/115/105/55 where your validator proves them), with explicit refusal for ASTC/cube/3D/array/MS/mips until you expose them. We must never map an unknown format to BGRA8 (current gd_format default does that in render; do not repeat it in the shared helper). If you have no API by the time I need it, I will implement the same subset privately in nord2_compute_resources.* and later switch to yours; please tell me now which names you will freeze, and whether you want my private packer deleted/aliased in integration.
